{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith","id":1546901,"title":"Do Inquisitor's in Dark Age actually use True Faith?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-12T07:55:26-08:00","id":1546901,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Do Inquisitor's in Dark Age actually use True Faith?","content":"To preface: I'm going to be biased in this discussion because mind is already leaning on &quot;probably no&quot;.<br /> <br /> The mechanics of DA: Inquisitor don't line up with any version of true faith in any edition. They focus entirely on Virtues rather than anything to do with the Willpower accotiation universal to every version of TF, reserve the classic &quot;repel vampires&quot; type powers to high levels despite that being the First power of TF, and inquisitors don't even need to be particularly faithful to have their powers despite TF's classically strict requirements.<br /> <br /> The one thing they do kind of line up with are HtR if hunters had access to a handful of Sorcerer paths and were forced to follow a version of the Road of Heaven from DA:Vampire.<br /> <br /> Question is, if Inquisitors aren't running with TF, what are they using? What are you thoughts?<br /> <br /> Personal Speculation: it could be they're proto-hunters created and managed by Lucifer. It's a thing in DtF and HtR lore that he was active during this time and he Really doesn't like supernaturals.<br /> The Inquisitors being Lucy's Gourmet version of the hunter recipe also fits his MO. She always does things Big when she's directly involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-12T08:15:17-08:00","id":1546902,"title":"","content":"I would say no too. I think a handful of Inquisitors actually do have True Faith, but the standard Inquisitor powers feel more like Numina to me. I like your theory though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-12T11:02:04-08:00","id":1546905,"title":"","content":"Yes and no?<br /> <br /> Yes, True Faith is canonically the power behind the abilities of the Inquisitors. They can only do what they do because of the fact that Faith can manifest into real power in the WoD; even if some of them rely on borrowed faith via relics instead of their own powerful faith.<br /> <br /> No, their mechanics don't line up at all with how other books apply True Faith, and yes were largely inspired by HtR despite not actually working like Edges either. There's a lot of reasons for this, but the DA Revised era books were not particularly worried about cross-compatibility with the rest of the WoD. DA Mage and DA Fae also work wildly differently from how the same powers are shown in other books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-12T12:59:13-08:00","id":1546906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1546905#post1546905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes and no?<br /> <br /> Yes, True Faith is canonically the power behind the abilities of the Inquisitors. They can only do what they do because of the fact that Faith can manifest into real power in the WoD; even if some of them rely on borrowed faith via relics instead of their own powerful faith.<br /> <br /> No, their mechanics don't line up at all with how other books apply True Faith, and yes were largely inspired by HtR despite not actually working like Edges either. There's a lot of reasons for this, but the DA Revised era books were not particularly worried about cross-compatibility with the rest of the WoD. DA Mage and DA Fae also work wildly differently from how the same powers are shown in other books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I already understand the Doylist perspective, but I'm more interested in the Warsonian speculation.<br /> <br /> Every DA gameline got a rundown on how they connect to each other and progress into the modern nights in books like Darkening Skies or Sorcerer's Crusade. DA: Inquisitor is actually special in that it's disjointed from how TF works, not just in the modern era, but also other games in the same DA line.<br /> <br /> So I want to ask, Why? Inquisitors seem to be Related to faith, but I is it actually capital F, True Faith or lower-case f like what powers blood magic or sorcerous numina?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-12T14:42:58-08:00","id":1546908,"title":"","content":"From a purely Watsonian approach?<br /> <br /> The Church, having organized faith based hunters on a scale never seen before, studied and refined True Faith into more distinct practices than &quot;wild&quot; True Faith that crops up in the wider human populace or even occasional supernatural entity. As the Inquisition lost power and status over time, it grew harder and harder to maintain these practices and eventually the Society of Leopold was forced to rely on True Faith however it manifested in order to have access to it at all to continue their fight against monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-13T10:17:41-08:00","id":1546929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1546908#post1546908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a purely Watsonian approach?<br /> <br /> The Church, having organized faith based hunters on a scale never seen before, studied and refined True Faith into more distinct practices than &quot;wild&quot; True Faith that crops up in the wider human populace or even occasional supernatural entity. As the Inquisition lost power and status over time, it grew harder and harder to maintain these practices and eventually the Society of Leopold was forced to rely on True Faith however it manifested in order to have access to it at all to continue their fight against monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>From you version, why are inquisitors without faith able to use that power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-13T14:42:02-08:00","id":1546932,"title":"","content":"I don't entirely agree with the proposition that inquisitors with no faith are able to make use of that power, just that there are ways for those of powerful faith to lend their power to those that cannot manifest faith based miracles on their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-13T15:23:18-08:00","id":1546933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1546932#post1546932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't entirely agree with the proposition that inquisitors with no faith are able to make use of that power, just that there are ways for those of powerful faith to lend their power to those that cannot manifest faith based miracles on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the book. Piety 0 Inquisitors are a thing and they don't lose any power, be it in superior virtue or endowments. It's even part of the narrative, not just a mechanical weirdness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-13T17:45:35-08:00","id":1546945,"title":"","content":"Piety 0 doesn't mean a character doesn't have faith, it means they've sinned against their code severely, and repeatedly, and have failed to repent for those misdeeds. The fact that you can have low Piety and a high rating in the Faith Superior Virtue is more than enough indication from the book that, getting back to the Watsonian perspective, that being an utter failure at abiding by the Church's teachings doesn't inherently mean you have no faith to speak of. The Inquisition might try to do what it can through indoctrination, but the life of an inquisitor is bound to lead to moments where dedication to the Inquisition, dedication to the Church, and dedication to the Lord come into conflict. Picking which you invest your faith in, in the moment, isn't the same as abandoning your faith totally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-13T19:08:46-08:00","id":1546946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1546945#post1546945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Piety 0 doesn't mean a character doesn't have faith, it means they've sinned against their code severely, and repeatedly, and have failed to repent for those misdeeds. The fact that you can have low Piety and a high rating in the Faith Superior Virtue is more than enough indication from the book that, getting back to the Watsonian perspective, that being an utter failure at abiding by the Church's teachings doesn't inherently mean you have no faith to speak of. The Inquisition might try to do what it can through indoctrination, but the life of an inquisitor is bound to lead to moments where dedication to the Inquisition, dedication to the Church, and dedication to the Lord come into conflict. Picking which you invest your faith in, in the moment, isn't the same as abandoning your faith totally.</div> </div> </div> </div>That goes against every single definition of True Faith in every splat. A consistent part of having True Faith isn't just having faith, you have to practice before the &quot;true&quot; half of it starts coming online. Inquisitors being fully able to become callous monsters that do whatever they want and still keep their powers flies in the face of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-13T22:22:54-08:00","id":1546953,"title":"","content":"OK, this is a bit frustrating because you're asking for exploring things from a Watsonian perspective, and then constantly bringing up Doyleist critiques. Which are we discussing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-13T23:18:35-08:00","id":1546954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1546946#post1546946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That goes against every single definition of True Faith in every splat. A consistent part of having True Faith isn't just having faith, you have to practice before the &quot;true&quot; half of it starts coming online. Inquisitors being fully able to become callous monsters that do whatever they want and still keep their powers flies in the face of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably only for Vampire and its extremely Christian assumptions about it (even V20 doesn't seem to spare much of a thought for anyone else, still requiring that licks have Humanity 9 to get it). But even then, I don't think that mortals have to meet Humanity minimums in order to get or keep TF, and you certainly don't need them in games that don't track Humanity, which is everyone that isn't Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T02:09:16-08:00","id":1546956,"title":"","content":"DAI is also explicit about something: it's version of True Faith is the &quot;full&quot; version where other games use a simplified version for their own purposes, like VtM games using Celerity when stating up Lupines instead of giving them Rage and explaining all the Rage rules. True Faith in the other games is a simple version for making antagonists. The far more complex powers in DAI are full rules for a game where everyone bases their power on faith. That's the official explanation in the rules for why things are different. But as a design device instead of an in-game explanation, if someone wants to explain the differences when has to best fit in an explanation for the extreme differences that come out of the abstraction of True Faith in the other games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T09:45:13-08:00","id":1546968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1546954#post1546954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably only for Vampire and its extremely Christian assumptions about it (even V20 doesn't seem to spare much of a thought for anyone else, still requiring that licks have Humanity 9 to get it). But even then, I don't think that mortals have to meet Humanity minimums in order to get or keep TF, and you certainly don't need them in games that don't track Humanity, which is everyone that isn't Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about humanity requirements(which don't apply outside VtM), I'm talking about the TF rating itself. TF has strict role-play requirements in any version I've seen, players transgressing against their faith lose Permanent dots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1546956#post1546956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DAI is also explicit about something: it's version of True Faith is the &quot;full&quot; version where other games use a simplified version for their own purposes, like VtM games using Celerity when stating up Lupines instead of giving them Rage and explaining all the Rage rules. True Faith in the other games is a simple version for making antagonists. The far more complex powers in DAI are full rules for a game where everyone bases their power on faith. That's the official explanation in the rules for why things are different. But as a design device instead of an in-game explanation, if someone wants to explain the differences when has to best fit in an explanation for the extreme differences that come out of the abstraction of True Faith in the other games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does it say that? If so, this might be one of the cases where I have to disagree with the book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T13:51:05-08:00","id":1546994,"title":"","content":"Page 158, in the sidebar conveniently titled &quot;True Faith.&quot;<br /> <br /> And if you want to disagree with the book, that's your decision, but that's the stance of the books. TF is a quick abstraction, DAI is a full system, but they're actually both the same thing in-universe. That is, ultimately, the Watsonian answer: DAI is the power of faith in all its variety and possibilities, while True Faith is a snippet as perceived by others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T15:05:48-08:00","id":1547004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1546994#post1546994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 158, in the sidebar conveniently titled &quot;True Faith.&quot;<br /> <br /> And if you want to disagree with the book, that's your decision, but that's the stance of the books. TF is a quick abstraction, DAI is a full system, but they're actually both the same thing in-universe. That is, ultimately, the Watsonian answer: DAI is the power of faith in all its variety and possibilities, while True Faith is a snippet as perceived by others.</div> </div> </div> </div>That conflicts with other things like Mummy and Sorcerer though. One of the things Mummy does is make True Faith and balance equivalent, and also establishes an equivalence between True Faith/Balance with the Mana background in sorcerer.<br /> <br /> One could make an argument for &quot;Separate Universes&quot; like they were pushing late second edition, but there's essentially two completely different splats that have opposed perspectives on TF while also using it as their main supernatural stat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T17:34:33-08:00","id":1547010,"title":"","content":"If you'd like me to sit here and list all the WoD books that contradict each other, I can, but it feels like a massive waste of time.<br /> <br /> I do think that the claim that Mummy makes True Faith and Balance the same thing is a big stretch, and it gets even bigger to claim that the Mana Background in Sorcerer is the same as either (esp. when Mummy follows more that Shekem and Quintessence are basically the same thing, and various supernatural power points are just specialized versions of those more primordial forms of magical power).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T18:05:08-08:00","id":1547013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1547004#post1547004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That conflicts with other things like Mummy and Sorcerer though. One of the things Mummy does is make True Faith and balance equivalent, and also establishes an equivalence between True Faith/Balance with the Mana background in sorcerer.<br /> <br /> One could make an argument for &quot;Separate Universes&quot; like they were pushing late second edition, but there's essentially two completely different splats that have opposed perspectives on TF while also using it as their main supernatural stat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's easily covered as &quot;every square is a rectangle but not every rectangle is a square&quot;. Balance is a potential form of TF. TF, unfortunately, can also encompass being Tomas de Torquemada, among other examples of fanatic clerics who do cruel and terrible things in the name of their faith, and we're not going to run out of supporting examples on this front any time soon, unfortunately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T19:00:23-08:00","id":1547016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1547013#post1547013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's easily covered as &quot;every square is a rectangle but not every rectangle is a square&quot;. Balance is a potential form of TF. TF, unfortunately, can also encompass being Tomas de Torquemada, among other examples of fanatic clerics who do cruel and terrible things in the name of their faith, and we're not going to run out of supporting examples on this front any time soon, unfortunately.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Fair. Ever since Mage first came out, they've been inserting &quot;paradigm&quot; into things outside of mage that didn't use to operate that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T19:42:05-08:00","id":1547018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1547016#post1547016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...Fair. Ever since Mage first came out, they've been inserting &quot;paradigm&quot; into things outside of mage that didn't use to operate that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, the Celerity vs Rage/Lupine vs Garou comparison that Heavy Arms mentioned still holds. The books have been full of mechanical kludges that got replaced over the years, even if it took a while for it to happen, sometimes - KotE describing Shih powers as Hungry Dead Disciplines but then switching to Qiao, Middle Dragons all having Galliard and one other Garou Auspice Gift access before the Mokole Breed Book, and the vast differences between fomori meant to be PCs (if short-lived ones) and fomori built as the ST needs them, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T03:48:04-08:00","id":1547054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1547010#post1547010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you'd like me to sit here and list all the WoD books that contradict each other, I can, but it feels like a massive waste of time.<br /> <br /> I do think that the claim that Mummy makes True Faith and Balance the same thing is a big stretch, and it gets even bigger to claim that the Mana Background in Sorcerer is the same as either (esp. when Mummy follows more that Shekem and Quintessence are basically the same thing, and various supernatural power points are just specialized versions of those more primordial forms of magical power).</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Mana and Shekem are more like Quint than TF, thus they are forms of static magic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-20T09:24:49-08:00","id":1547163,"title":"","content":"One thing that bothered me about the Inquisitor game is the way it glorified the real Inquisition, which tortured and killed heretics and non-Christians by the thousands in medieval times. Yes, I know that the Shadow Inquisition that the PC Inquisitors belong to is not the same as the real Inquisition, but the similarities still bother me a little.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-20T11:49:23-08:00","id":1547167,"title":"","content":"It's a bit of a tight-rope to walk given that at the point in time of DA Revised, the worst atrocities carried out under the banner of inquisition (keeping in mind that in reality there was no &quot;the&quot; Inquisition, like the Crusades each was a singular event using the same Church process) hadn't happened yet. At this point in history, the official inquisitions had no authority to punish people outside of ordering penance or at worst excommunication from the Church. It was up to local law as to what would happen after the Church declared a defendant guilty of heresy or apostasy; and in many places that couldn't even be charged against non-Christians since it's hard to betray a religion you're not part of.<br /> <br /> Over time, the inquisitions got heavier handed (and more centralized from Rome) because they never really addressed all the flaws in the Church that would culminate in the Reformation. Persuasion failed after hypocrisy was revealed, advisement to kings and magistrates failed after it was clear they were acting in self-interest, etc. But rather than fixing itself, the Church increasingly tried harsher force to put down dissent. <br /> <br /> I'm not going to say the glorification criticism is baseless, but the problem for me lies a lot more in not addressing where the real world history of the practice of inquisition was, and where it was headed. Since most people are far more familiar with the inquisitions that hadn't happened yet from the start date of DA Rev, not giving that context comes off as more apologetic towards those events rather than playing into the flaws of the Shadow Inquisition and it's own issues with zealotry and callousness. It would have actually helped the book to get a bit more historical instead of pop-culture in that regard, because the start of the inquisitions was by not means innocent but it was sympathetic. Whether the institution would end up centuries later is very in keeping with the Shadow Inquisitions own fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-20T20:25:59-08:00","id":1547172,"title":"","content":"Here's my head canon of WHY dark ages Inquisitors powers are so different, but similar to Edges and don't show up in the modern nights. It's also...wickedly ironic for the world of darkness.<br /> <br /> The Dark Ages powers comes from Lucifer empowering them. Now hear me out. We know the Imbued and their edges comes from the last two angels in the modern nights. Around this time in the Dark Ages canon, Lucifer is wagging a war against the earthbound by promoting the Church to deny them of faith and make them slumber. Since Lucifer never fell, he's also still an Angel. Thus he is the secret source of the Dark Ages Inquisitors powers during this time. Even the church doesn't know it, they think it's just faith given by God. It was all part of a secret plan to defeat the earthbound at the time that got out of control (as these things often do in the world of darkness.)<br /> <br /> That's my personal preference for an explanation anyways why Dark Ages Inquisitors have different powers but are very similar to Edges and the Imbued.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-21T03:10:11-08:00","id":1547175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1547172#post1547172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's my head canon of WHY dark ages Inquisitors powers are so different, but similar to Edges and don't show up in the modern nights. It's also...wickedly ironic for the world of darkness.<br /> <br /> The Dark Ages powers comes from Lucifer empowering them. Now hear me out. We know the Imbued and their edges comes from the last two angels in the modern nights. Around this time in the Dark Ages canon, Lucifer is wagging a war against the earthbound by promoting the Church to deny them of faith and make them slumber. Since Lucifer never fell, he's also still an Angel. Thus he is the secret source of the Dark Ages Inquisitors powers during this time. Even the church doesn't know it, they think it's just faith given by God. It was all part of a secret plan to defeat the earthbound at the time that got out of control (as these things often do in the world of darkness.)<br /> <br /> That's my personal preference for an explanation anyways why Dark Ages Inquisitors have different powers but are very similar to Edges and the Imbued.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes a lot of sense! I like that better than their powers being derived from True Faith. True Faith is supposed to be really rare and shouldn\u2019t be available to all members of an order, even a super secret order like the Shadow Inquisition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-21T14:20:35-08:00","id":1547180,"title":"","content":"It's not a bad headcanon from a broad perspective, but it's the exact opposite of Lucifer's efforts according to the books. Lucifer was sabotaging religion to decrease faith - the food of the Earthbound - as any faith makes his enemies stronger. Humorously, Lucifer loves the modern Church of Satan because they basically 100% got his message without a system of worshiping him. It makes far more sense for the Earthbound to be behind things since they have a limitless supply of demons in the abyss to let the Inquisition defeat, while in the process promoting faith, superstition, conflict, and inequality among humans.<br /> <br /> Though both are things that tend to get under a lot of people's skin when it comes to Demon and the whole &quot;It was Lucifer all along,&quot; thing, as it diminishes so much of the WoD's potential for thematic stories when it turns out everything was just part of Lucifer's post-rebellion plot. Nobody playing an Inquisitor in the WoD is expecting to smash demons with faith as pure power fantasy: the game wants you to confront the Church's excesses as much as supernatural monsters. &quot;You're not actually using the power of faith, you're just a secret pawn of Satan,&quot; isn't really good for playing the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-21T22:40:36-08:00","id":1547183,"title":"","content":"Part of my brain is going with a thing from the old Ravenloft setting where divine casters apparently got cut off from their gods upon entering the land of mists/demiplane of dread but still got those powers because something else was providing them. So could be that some of the inquisitors are managing to sync up with <i>something</i> enabling them to replicate the effects that isn't the same as what would be fueling the same merit in a modern game. Not in the same way as the dread powers in Ravenloft, but more like those stories where the person gets their coffee brand switched out on them and doesn't notice because its in the same container.<br /> <br /> Granted this could also just be because my first thought was just that for whatever reasons it may have just been easier to tap the force that counts for true faith then in modern settings. Just my musing on an in universe explanation if you were dealing with someone who'd been around long enough to notice things. Not counting that my example includes game lines they probably wouldn't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-22T07:52:26-08:00","id":1547187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1547180#post1547180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a bad headcanon from a broad perspective, but it's the exact opposite of Lucifer's efforts according to the books. Lucifer was sabotaging religion to decrease faith - the food of the Earthbound</div> </div> </div> </div>In the first part of the DtF books, it explicitly paints the rise of abrahamic faiths as lucifer's direct doing. Earthbound can't harvest from abrahamic faith like they were from pantheistic faiths because it's directed at capital G.<br /> <br /> Lucifer only started killing off abrahamic faith(hinted to be in league with, or a shadowy benefactor of, the order of reason) After the earthbound were dealt with(around the enlightenment era)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-22T11:54:34-08:00","id":1547188,"title":"","content":"Um, the Earthbound can feed off of any source of faith. Lucifer might have originally thought promoting Abrahamic religions would stop them, but he was wrong (also the pre-Christian Roman empire did a lot of damage to the Earthbound on their own), as it only slowed them down by making gaining faith more complicated instead of impossible. The Earthbounds' biggest weakness is that they have a much more restricted form of harvesting faith, and generally need to rely on weaker demons or existing Thrall cults to corrupt people into performing specific rituals instead of whatever expression of faith like modern Fallen can reap from. A human can fully belief they're worshiping Jesus while actually performing a rite to Belial, and it will feed the archduke.<br /> <br /> The Eartbound were largely nullified until the Dark Ages because it was easier to keep them in check with a well organized empire that doesn't practice the binding rituals Lucifer taught the ancient Mesopotamian cultures hoping it would free his friends and they could restart; not realizing the resentment they would have directly at him for not being sent to the Abyss as well despite him breaking them out as fast as he could. It was the ascendancy of Christianity and Islam into secular power instead of just being spiritual movements that made them open to the mundane temptation of corruption and power that let infernalism spread again, to which Lucifer countered with reformist movements (groups the Inquisition actively suppresses) and eventually starting fully pushing for the Enlightenment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-22T14:31:37-08:00","id":1547191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1547188#post1547188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, the Earthbound can feed off of any source of faith.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Both DtF earthbound and Devil's Due disagree with you here. They disagree on the source of Why earthbound cannot harvest from abrahamic faith(DtF:E claims it's because Lucifer is the one powering abrahamic faith while DD claims it's because Capital G is the one doing it), but they both agree on the outcome.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-23T13:31:08-08:00","id":1547206,"title":"","content":"OK, I don't have the DtF stuff on digital files, so it's a bit hard for me to dig through all the books the old fashioned way. So can you tell me what pages you're looking at? Because I crack open the books, physically, and don't see it.<br /> <br /> DD (which in the same section specifically mentions that Lucifer is trying to take down the Church), doesn't say that demons can't feed from Abrahamic faith, just that in the DA era faith is, in general, harder to harvest than it was in the past; requiring a larger amount of offerings from humans where one used to be enough. The closest it gets to pointing to who's responsible is it says that the longer things stray from the time of Adam and Eve where humans and the Heavenly Host walked side by side, the weaker humanity's power of faith has gotten because the divine is less and less absent in their lives. There is a line about faith in the Lord not being the same as faith in a demonic master, but that doesn't really change anything; non-Eartbound demons can siphon off of any faith by the regaining Resolve rules, and Earthbound are limited to gaining Resolve from getting people to do specific rituals performed for them which can be accomplished via deception and overwhelming mortals with former-Angel powers. Earthbound can't just sit around in a holy place of any religion or culture and sup on faith. The process of binding themselves into a vessel to resist the Abyss cuts them off from what free-roaming and human-possessing demons can take advantage of.<br /> <br /> The book also really don't jive with the idea that Abrahamic faiths in general are special because it calls out Europe as being special, while Africa and Asia have plenty of people of multiple branches of Abrahamic tradition (including a bunch of smaller groups besides the big three), but are apparently just as easy to get faith off of as polytheists and ancestor worshipers. Being a Coptic Christian in Egypt apparently doesn't help you against demons try to use you for food, but being a Moorish Muslim in Spain does.<br /> <br /> So... yeah... just being told &quot;the books disagree with me,&quot; is a bit grating. I'm reading the books. It's hard for me to C&amp;P directly from DD or Earthbound, but it feels like we're looking at completely different texts. While it's entirely possible the books have internal inconsistencies, in fact the absolutely do between DA and modern times, I really am not finding what passages you think are so conclusive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-29T11:15:16-08:00","id":1547307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1547206#post1547206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, I don't have the DtF stuff on digital files, so it's a bit hard for me to dig through all the books the old fashioned way. So can you tell me what pages you're looking at? Because I crack open the books, physically, and don't see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bit late because chirstmas, but:<br /> <br /> In DtF: Earthbound at the section &quot;Tribes of Men&quot; on page 22, through &quot;Christianity&quot; on page 29, and continuing all the way to page 37(there's even a sidebar on buddhism outlining that it had a similar effect).<br /> <br /> For DD, It starts on page 25 &quot;Rise of Christianity&quot; and continues all the way to page 28.<br /> <br /> The entire reason the earthbound are losing power and why their cults of faith are shrinking is because of the rise of abrahamic faiths, Especially Christianity and Islam.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1547206#post1547206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DD (which in the same section specifically mentions that Lucifer is trying to take down the Church)</div> </div> </div> </div>Weirdly enough, DtF: Earthbound links christianity itself and the catholic church to being &quot;Stamped by Lucifer&quot;. Combined that with some things from &quot;Fair is Foul&quot; in VtM ToJ: Gehenna, and it sets up a serious argument that Lucifer is the &quot;God&quot; fueling the powers of True Faith in WoD's setting. DD is written from the perspective of the shadow-inquisition, who definitely wouldn't be in the know if their god was in fact as mask lucifer was wearing.<br /> <br /> This also has historical precedent. Gnosticism was started partly because discrepancies between the actions of the old and new testament versions of god lead some christians t believe they were separate entities and that one of them was actually an imposter tricking abrahamics into submitting to them(though, there was disagreements on which, what, who, where, and why).<br /> <br /> However, DD has him destroying Constantinople for some reason. While the Catholic-church ties thing isn't affected by this, it might show there's a divide and lucifer isn't behind all of christianity so much as has infiltrated it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1547206#post1547206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">while Africa and Asia have plenty of people of multiple branches of Abrahamic tradition (including a bunch of smaller groups besides the big three), but are apparently just as easy to get faith off of as polytheists and ancestor worshipers.</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't as easy though? Demons are being/had already been fought back and are losing/had lost power there too. Even Asia is losing/has lost it's demonic overlords because of the rise of buddhism.<br /> <br /> Europe isn't really special by any measure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-29T14:59:27-08:00","id":1547312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1547307#post1547307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The entire reason the earthbound are losing power and why their cults of faith are shrinking is because of the rise of abrahamic faiths, Especially Christianity and Islam.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was, they've been fighting back and all.<br /> <br /> As well, this is a bit of a goalpost shift from &quot;Earthbound can't get Faith from Abrahamic people,&quot; to, &quot;the rise of Abrahamic religion reduced the Earthbound's practical power.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Weirdly enough, DtF: Earthbound links christianity itself and the catholic church to being &quot;Stamped by Lucifer&quot;. </div> </div> </div>It says that, like Jews before them, Christians were stamped by Lucifer's influence. The book doesn't say anything about Lucifer giving his &quot;stamp&quot; to the Catholic Church.<br /> <br /> It also says that the Abrahamic faiths were potent in blessings from the Creator <i>before</i> Lucifer found them. Lucifer only guided them from afar because they already had what he was looking for; he didn't need to directly do anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Combined that with some things from &quot;Fair is Foul&quot; in VtM ToJ: Gehenna, and it sets up a serious argument that Lucifer is the &quot;God&quot; fueling the powers of True Faith in WoD's setting. </div> </div> </div>The Fair is Foul scenario is (a) an optional scenario and (b) explicit in that its depiction of Lucifer contradicts DtF's take on the Morningstar. Basing a theory off this doesn't really mean much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> DD is written from the perspective of the shadow-inquisition, who definitely wouldn't be in the know if their god was in fact as mask lucifer was wearing. </div> </div> </div>It explicitly is not. The fiction is from the perspective of a demon, and the book is written broadly as a source-book for either running DtF style demons in DA, or to supplement any of the DA games. There's a whole section in the back about how to use the book for any DA game. There's all sorts of things in the book that the shadow inquisition knows nothing about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gnosticism was started partly because discrepancies between the actions of the old and new testament versions of god lead some christians t believe they were separate entities and that one of them was actually an imposter tricking abrahamics into submitting to them(though, there was disagreements on which, what, who, where, and why). </div> </div> </div>Gnosticism predates Christianity, as it emerged out of late Hellenistic and early Roman mystery cults intermingling with Zoroastrians. Gnostic Judaism and Gnostic Christianity had a moment in the spotlight as Christianity was starting to form it's own identity, but both fell out of favor with their respective religions as forms of esoteric and mystic thought that weren't so contradictory with mainstream canonical beliefs became more prominent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, DD has him destroying Constantinople for some reason. </div> </div> </div>No, it says his fingerprints where on it, and he called the attention of all the other demons to it. Consider that at this point in the timeline there are considerably more than the 666 Earthbound that were heavily opposed to Lucifer, and many more fallen running around forming their own opinions that hadn't be part of all of the squabbling until recently. It's not really hard to see this as an attempt by Lucifer to undercut the Earthbound's authority over most of their followers among the demonic ranks and try to get them to instead follow Lucifer's ways<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They aren't as easy though? Demons are being/had already been fought back and are losing/had lost power there too. Even Asia is losing/has lost it's demonic overlords because of the rise of buddhism.<br /> <br /> Europe isn't really special by any measure. </div> </div> </div>DD, p. 32-33: &quot;(Things are different outside Europe, where the Church has no influence and faith in the pagan gods remains strong. Europe has become the focus of demonic activity in the Dark Medieval, the place where so many demons flocked during the rise of the Roman Empire. Those Hell-born who infest the rest of the world can draw on greater reserves of faith and power, but are badly outnumbered by their European rivals. For their own safety, these outsiders keep their own council and rarely interfere with events in Europe, lest their desperate brethren tear them apart for their War against the angels, and it was when humanity finally rejected the lies and horrors of the demons that the Host were able to defeat them and condemn them to Hell.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, in DD, Europe is special.<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> Broadly, it really feels like you're taking a bunch of suggestions, implications, story hooks, and in-character unreliable narrators and picking a specific theory from that. By itself that's not a problem, but it's not the same as what the official stance of the books is supposed to be. Basically, you're insisting that &quot;X is true&quot; based on a bunch of things that just say, &quot;X might be true,&quot; while ignoring all the evidence that &quot;X isn't true&quot; present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-29T20:27:15-08:00","id":1547323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1547312#post1547312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was, they've been fighting back and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1547312#post1547312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well, this is a bit of a goalpost shift from &quot;Earthbound can't get Faith from Abrahamic people,&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>*Abrahamic <i>Faith</i>. Not people. Big distinction.<br /> The earthbound are able to masquerade as the gods of many religions to harvest faith, Abrahamic faiths(and Buddhism) are not one of them. That is and has always been my point. My argument has not changed, goalposts have not been moved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1547312#post1547312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It says that, like Jews before them, Christians were stamped by Lucifer's influence. The book doesn't say anything about Lucifer giving his &quot;stamp&quot; to the Catholic Church.<br /> <br /> It also says that the Abrahamic faiths were potent in blessings from the Creator <i>before</i> Lucifer found them. Lucifer only guided them from afar because they already had what he was looking for; he didn't need to directly do anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that's arguable either way<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1547312#post1547312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fair is Foul scenario is (a) an optional scenario and (b) explicit in that its depiction of Lucifer contradicts DtF's take on the Morningstar. Basing a theory off this doesn't really mean much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair.<br /> Lilith also spread a story that she was God's consort after being banished by said god from the garden, so her version of events aren't necessarily reliable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1547312#post1547312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> It explicitly is not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mistype on my part. I meant DA: Inquisition, not DD<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1547312#post1547312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Gnosticism predates Christianity</div> </div> </div> </div>You're going to have to specify the &quot;gnosticism&quot; you mean. I was talking about the movement that included apostle john getting visions of jesus expaining the cosmology of the demiurge to him. That version obviously couldn't have predated christianity by any measure.<br /> I hate the fact historians put a collections of loosely related religions under one label and pretended they were the same.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1547312#post1547312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> No, it says his fingerprints where on it, and he called the attention of all the other demons to it. Consider that at this point in the timeline there are considerably more than the 666 Earthbound that were heavily opposed to Lucifer, and many more fallen running around forming their own opinions that hadn't be part of all of the squabbling until recently. It's not really hard to see this as an attempt by Lucifer to undercut the Earthbound's authority over most of their followers among the demonic ranks and try to get them to instead follow Lucifer's ways</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not following. How does the destruction of constantinople and megaphone of &quot;god is gone and we remain&quot;(paraphrasing) contribute to what you just said?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1547312#post1547312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> DD, p. 32-33: &quot;(Things are different outside Europe, <b>where the Church has no influence</b> and faith in the pagan gods remains strong. Europe has become the focus of demonic activity in the Dark Medieval, the place where so many demons flocked during the rise of the Roman Empire. Those Hell-born who infest the rest of the world can draw on greater reserves of faith and power, but are badly outnumbered by their European rivals. For their own safety, these outsiders keep their own council and rarely interfere with events in Europe, lest their desperate brethren tear them apart for their War against the angels, and it was when humanity finally rejected the lies and horrors of the demons that the Host were able to defeat them and condemn them to Hell.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, in DD, Europe is special.</div> </div> </div> </div>The paragraph you just outlined explains what I was trying to convey. Europe isn't special because its europe. It's different because it's got a larger distribution of christian infleunce than other parts of the world.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1547312#post1547312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200b<br /> Broadly, it really feels like you're taking a bunch of suggestions, implications, story hooks, and in-character unreliable narrators and picking a specific theory from that. By itself that's not a problem, but it's not the same as what the official stance of the books is supposed to be. Basically, you're insisting that &quot;X is true&quot; based on a bunch of things that just say, &quot;X might be true,&quot; while ignoring all the evidence that &quot;X isn't true&quot; present.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like you're misconstruing what I said and are arguing against that instead of my actual point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-30T00:54:45-08:00","id":1547324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1547323#post1547323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Abrahamic <i>Faith</i>. Not people. Big distinction.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that this doesn't apply to the non-Earthbound is a big point you're not addressing, also:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The earthbound are able to masquerade as the gods of many religions to harvest faith, Abrahamic faiths(and Buddhism) are not one of them. </div> </div> </div>No, they aren't. Earthbound in DA and DtF, are only capable of gaining faith from rituals specifically dedicated to them. The process of becoming earthbound forces them to rely on direct worship regardless of who the worship is from. It doesn't matter if someone was raised in Christian belief or Taoist belief, an earthbound has to convince them (generally through deception or corruption) to direct their worship to the earthbound in question instead of to their normal entities of veneration.<br /> <br /> So:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is and has always been my point. </div> </div> </div>This doesn't make any sense.<br /> <br /> It's also just not what the books broadly get at. The influence of different religions (and why the Abrahamic traditions have an advantage but aren't actually unique) is on how a culture normalizes different expressions of faith.<br /> <br /> That's why the Roman state religion is posed as a bad time for the earthbound, but a bounty for the other demons: the Roman state religion was based on Roman supremacy; so devotions to other peoples' deities was taboo (compared to the Hellenistic culture started by Alexander the Great who decided to start mingling Greek and local practices freely, making them far easier to convince to make offerings to the earthbound as just another local deity to offer up a sacrifice too). However, the Roman state religion was still a very powerful institution and thus there was plenty of faith flowing around for the demons that weren't constrained by binding to harvest from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My argument has not changed, goalposts have not been moved. </div> </div> </div>Your original phrasing was, &quot;Earthbound can't harvest from abrahamic faith like they were from pantheistic faiths because it's directed at capital G.&quot; So yes, the goal posts have moved. Buddhists don't direct their faith to the capital G either, but you keep bringing them up as a philosophy that works against the earthbound, which undermines the idea that direct worship of the big G is part of the core issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd say that's arguable either way </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure you can either &quot;either way&quot; on if the Catholic Church specifically has Lucifer's stamp of approval. Either the books actually directly say he does, or the fact that the books directly say he's been seeking to diminish the power of the Church means it is not very arguable that the shadow inquisition has Lucifer's approval (which started all of this tangent to be clear) via approval over the Catholic Church.<br /> <br /> I'm also not sure where the &quot;either way&quot; part of Lucifer's influence on Judaism, and later Christianity (and for one assumes Islam even if for whatever reasons the books avoid Islam as much as possible in this regard) being indirect. That's what the books say. He planned on taking a more active hand, and found a tribe of humans that were already where he was hoping to guide a group too. That's what the texts cited say about it. What is there to argue in a different direction?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mistype on my part. I meant DA: Inquisition, not DD </div> </div> </div>OK... but I have no idea what this means now because it wasn't a response to a reference to anything in DAI.<br /> <br /> I said, &quot;DD said X.&quot;<br /> You responded with, &quot;DD is written from an inquisitor perspective.&quot;<br /> I said, &quot;DD is not.&quot;<br /> You clarified, &quot;I meant DAI.&quot;<br /> <br /> So... yeah, where's this meant to go? You've made a specific sentence logical at the cost of the coherence of the rest of the passage. I'm not relying on anything DAI said to make my case, nor have you cited anything from DAI that adds to that point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're going to have to specify the &quot;gnosticism&quot; you mean. I was talking about the movement that included apostle john getting visions of jesus expaining the cosmology of the demiurge to him. That version obviously couldn't have predated christianity by any measure.<br /> I hate the fact historians put a collections of loosely related religions under one label and pretended they were the same. </div> </div> </div>Gnosticism has never been its own religion. And while it has varied wildly in specific practice as different religions have flirted with it, there's a fairly direct line from late Hellenistic merging of Zoroastrian beliefs with their own after Alexander got all enamored with Persian culture after conquering them, to late Temple era Jewish Gnosticism (including proto-Christian Gnosticism since that's where they got it from), to the early Christian Gnosticism that started doing things like using the division of the old and new testaments to divorce themselves more fully from their Jewish origins. It might not be one consistent philosophical movement, but this isn't some wild conflation of things separated by huge swathes of time and space.<br /> <br /> Proto-Christians and early Christian Gnostics didn't invent Gnosticism, they borrowed from it - or even fully incorporated it - to try to form a cohesive theology that justified expunging their Jewish theological roots.<br /> <br /> It's not exactly greet discussion rhetoric to both decry historians for lumping things together, and then say I need to be more specific about which form of Gnosticism I'm talking about when you didn't specify a form in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not following. How does the destruction of constantinople and megaphone of &quot;god is gone and we remain&quot;(paraphrasing) contribute to what you just said? </div> </div> </div>Again, the books never pin the destruction of Constantinople on Lucifer specifically (and larger WoD canon most certainly does not).<br /> <br /> Lucifer taking advantage of the the fall of Constantinople to turn on that megaphone is a way to circumvent the earthbound, and specifically the archdukes, that had been doing most of the spreading of demon summoning and infernalism in order to gain non-bound demons as allies who didn't even know if Lucifer was still around and only had the archdukes and their existing servants to rely on. It was a chance to say, &quot;Hey, I'm still here, I'm still around, and the Rebellion against Heaven isn't over.&quot; I'm not sure why that doesn't fall into Lucifer's general WoD style, it's not like his plans have always been perfect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The paragraph you just outlined explains what I was trying to convey. Europe isn't special because its europe. It's different because it's got a larger distribution of christian infleunce than other parts of the world. </div> </div> </div>Europe isn't special because it's Europe, it's special because it's Christian, doesn't really make things better. Especially given that whole Islam thing (which during the period of the DA Rev games, has spread from Morocco to the Philippines).<br /> <br /> I get we're talking about gaming books here, but where exactly is this paradise for demons to get lots of faith from if Europe isn't special? If Islam and Buddhism are diminishing demons throughout Asia and North Africa... and there are organized religions in the rest of the world that aren't actually just like, &quot;wow a powerful spirit being, I must worship it regardless of my own beliefs,&quot; like the Buddhists manage to resist too... most of humanity is living under organized state religions by the Medieval era. Most people are not backwoods &quot;pagans&quot; (keeping in mind the origins of the word pagan) just because they're not from a small handful of religions. And every organized religion has taboos against making deals with evil spirits that teach people to be cautious in such matters (that's literally the point of fairy tales).<br /> <br /> Either Europe is special (even if just for being Christian dominated at this point in history), or the rest of the text about the rest of the world doesn't make any sense. Of course Europe being special doesn't actually make any sense in the first place, but it's a distinct problem with the DA Rev line in particular of trying to give in-universe reasons to focus on Europe. People would have been just fine if the authors said, &quot;we're focusing on Europe as supernatural European history is so influential on the modern nights of the WoD, but don't think that means stuff outside of Europe is lesser for it.&quot; and left it at that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like you're misconstruing what I said and are arguing against that instead of my actual point. </div> </div> </div>I'm open to the possibility of miscommunications leading to statements that aren't going over well happening here. However, it's not particularly useful to dodge the point about how you're treating the books as more directly stating your case than seems justifiable. Nor does it help to accuse me of misconstruing your points, when you have literally pulled, &quot;DtF says Europe isn't special, so your point that DD says Europe is special doesn't matter.&quot; How more of a direct example do I need of you doing exactly what you're saying I'm doing here?<br /> <br /> And let's be clear. Your point here is, fundamentally, that I'm wrong. This whole thing stemmed from my response to a different poster about their headcanon idea and some of the claims I made in it. When I defended it, you chose to nitpick one detail, and we've been arguing that for a page. And it that whole time you've yet to cite a single passage that actually states, &quot;Earthbound can't harvest from abrahamic faith like they were from pantheistic faiths because it's directed at capital G.&quot; As I've noted, repeatedly, the earthbound have more stringent feeding restrictions, but the faith of the individuals in question isn't part of that directly. Nothing in any of the pages you cited state otherwise.<br /> <br /> So, why not, clearly, state what your point is if I'm wrong about it, because beyond trying to claim I'm wrong via increasingly circuitous arguments, sure, I've lost completely track of what the goal of your posts are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-30T17:00:05-08:00","id":1547352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1547324#post1547324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, why not, clearly, state what your point is if I'm wrong about it, because beyond trying to claim I'm wrong via increasingly circuitous arguments, sure, I've lost completely track of what the goal of your posts are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather than writing an essay I'll just hit the important points:<br /> I was originally pointing out that lucifer was encouraging abrahamic faiths, long before he started sabataging them, when you stated that Lucifer's MO was always sabataging them(in your post responding to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3215_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3215\" data-vbnamecard=\"3215\">SuperSabbatST</a> theory). At minimum, DTF: Earthbound agrees with the my point here.<br /> <br /> We then went on to argue the particulars of the Why, as throughout this, you resisted the initial point that Lucifer was helping the christian faith in a way that would allow the &quot;Inquisition is powered by Lucifer&quot; theory to have any ground. I pointed to the fact earthbound were losing faith in the rise of abrahamic religions, made some assumptions as to why that was and pointed to DtF: Earthbound and DD as evidence.<br /> <br /> I also stand by the my assertion that earthbound could not harvest faith from abrahamic religions the way they could by grafting themselves into polytheistic religions. My understanding of Why may have been wrong(the fact buddhism works too is enough to Disprove God as a necessary component), but that original point hasn't changed.<br /> <br /> My point at the beginning of this discussion(lucifer aided the original abrahamic faiths) has also remained the same, some of the postulates on why I believed that point have been challenged by you, but not the original point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-30T17:44:37-08:00","id":1547356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546901-do-inquisitor-s-in-dark-age-actually-use-true-faith?p=1547352#post1547352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was originally pointing out that lucifer was encouraging abrahamic faiths, long before he started sabataging them, when you stated that Lucifer's MO was always sabataging them(in your post responding to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3215_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3215\" data-vbnamecard=\"3215\">SuperSabbatST</a> theory).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... a fairly tortured reading of my posts. I can see how you might have felt that way about my initial response, but on this point I've expanded a few times in a fashion that doesn't hold to this reading.<br /> <br /> What I've been saying, is that Lucifer has used religion repeatedly to forward his goals, and generally ends up working against those religions once his plans don't work out. He did it to the ancient faiths he taught demon summoning too to try to free the archdukes, and he did it to the Church by the time the DA Rev era has started. I was not trying to say that Lucifer was not involved with the Abrahamic faiths (though I do standby my assertion that the books clearly say he was more hands off with them than he was with others), just that like he has before, he sabotages what he's built when things don't go his way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We then went on to argue the particulars of the Why... </div> </div> </div>We really haven't been talking about this at all in most of the posts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...you resisted the initial point that Lucifer was helping the christian faith in a way that would allow the &quot;Inquisition is powered by Lucifer&quot; theory to have any ground. </div> </div> </div>And... the 1,000 years from early Christians to the &quot;now&quot; of DA is plenty of time for Lucifer's initial attempts to support Christians to have faded into working against the Church as another of his failures. Again, the books directly say that by the present of DA, Lucifer is working against the Church. If he's directly powering the shadow inquisition... he would just revoke that power if he's trying to sabotage them (which, again, the books say he is already).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also stand by the my assertion that earthbound could not harvest faith from abrahamic religions the way they could by grafting themselves into polytheistic religions. </div> </div> </div>You've yet to point to a single bit of evidence in support of this, and not address at all the books descriptions of how the earthbound feed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My point at the beginning of this discussion(lucifer aided the original abrahamic faiths) has also remained the same, some of the postulates on why I believed that point have been challenged by you, but not the original point. </div> </div> </div>What Lucifer was doing thousands of years ago doesn't really make much of a point to the idea that he's actively doing it now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-03T17:43:45-08:00","id":1548168,"title":"","content":"My guess is that the True Faith in Dark Ages: Inquisitor is a prelude to what would eventually become the Edges of the Imbued, and that The Messengers are merely the angels who remained loyal to God (tbh, I never cared for the &quot;Lucifer did it!&quot; explanations that Demon so often loved to promote) and since the Dark Ages was a time of both great strife and intense supernatural activity, the Heavenly Host began to empower certain pious individuals in larger numbers, but in a way that was different from the more &quot;organic&quot; True Faith seen in the modern era of Vampire: The Masquerade. <br /> <br /> Devil's Due might even tie into it a bit, as supposedly the Earthbound became more active during the medieval era and you had more infernalist cults like the Circle of the Red being highly active around that time as well.<br /> <br /> After the Inquisition and the Anarch Revolt ended The Long Night and faeries were forced to adopt the Changeling Way or fuck off to Arcadia full-time for the next several centuries, along with the general decline of Clan Baali and the Circle of Red during the Renaissance/Early Modern Period, the angels slowly backed away from gifting mortals with such power and only re-emerged after the Sixth Great Maelstrom, where they became known as The Messengers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-11T19:50:55-08:00","id":1548418,"title":"","content":"Which Inquisitor? There are several different-books: but you're talking about the red one with the dagger on it? I always just assumed they had some sort of faith or faith-magic to work their numina; the Messianic-Voices make better Inquisitors and they have faith-magic!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T20:48:03-08:00","id":1548651,"title":"","content":"Definitely. How else would the seek out heretics, witches and those who sold their soul to Wyrm/Nephandi? How else would they sense supernatural creatures. I would say DEFINITELY. Especially TRUE Inquisitors. Not the ones who join inquisiton for power and influence, but TRUE religious believers. And, remember in how many stories the inquisitor STRONGLY PRESENTS THE SIGN OF A CROSS and says &quot;BE GONE DEMON!!!&quot;. That can be only done with True Faith. Deus Vult!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26712-tigerclaw_x","name":"Tigerclaw_x","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}